[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS026
TITLE: Plan an airborne course from physics projections
STATEMENT: >>>
The Tower CSCI shall plan one aircraft's airborne course by projecting that aircraft and the surrounding aircraft with the C physics model. The plan shall satisfy the radar lateral minima, the vertical minima, and the classic wake minima, or it shall report the predicted loss. A course plan shall not be written to the issued runway clearance log. Acceptance is a same-altitude pair whose projection closes inside the lateral minimum and is given an altitude amendment, a pair already separated by 1,000 feet whose plan is to maintain, and a runway clearance log that stays empty.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The runway guard remains the only writer of an issued runway clearance. The airborne plan is a separate check over projected positions.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: High-Level
VERIFICATION: Test
ASSUMPTIONS: The minima are JO 7110.65BB Change 3, effective July 9, 2026, paragraphs 5-5-4 and 4-5-1. Notice N JO 7110.806 is not applied. The terminal antenna is the airport reference supplied with the flight. Fusion, STARS multi-sensor, an ERAM 3 NM area, MSSR out to 60 NM, MEARTS, and 2.5 NM on final are not selected. Wake uses super, heavy, B757, large, and small. Letters A through I are not assigned. A B757 follower uses the large-follower number where paragraph 5-5-4 names Large. Directly behind means aft of the leader and within 2,500 feet of its track. The check allows one foot and one thousandth of a mile for projection rounding. The planner amends only the subject aircraft and tries altitude, then heading, then speed. This is not a certification claim.
